ding sms texts all  over the place if you're doing  two-factor authentication  um a lot of  details around encryption and  you know managing managing the identity  properly  and this is also a super super standard  problem uh just about every web app has  this type of problem and so what that  means is there's a bunch of tools out  there that can provide authentication  services for you we happen to use amazon  cognito but there's octa google and  azure have their own identity and login  systems you can use single sign-in from  for instance github like the pi data  site does  there can also be gdpr implications you  know if you know a lot of personal  information about users then you need to  manage that properly  and all of these work uh mostly with  what's called a jwt token so i'll talk  about that in a little bit more depth  and so this is a nice way to separate  out the authentication from the rest of  your tool  next slide  so as i mentioned there's actually a lot  of complicated parts of authorization  also think about how do you freeze an  account how do you change access rights  you know you need interfaces and you  need ways to do all of this  in order to manage your users properly  next slide  so  other side of this is authorization so  now we're figuring out congratulations  you're bob are you allowed to see this  project uh are you allowed to edit it  are you allowed to view it are you  allowed to do you know are you allowed  to add uh make it much more complicated  does your license level allow you to do  that or do you need to pay more money  first  next slide  so to to give an example that we will  typically run into  uh there may be  uh our typical end user is for instance  a transit agency and they're planning  out their electric bus infrastructure  and so there may be a project and their  staff may be involved with that they may  also have a consulting firm involved  with that who can edit it  that we may be supporting the project  directly and so